{
  "id": "KS-HB-2437-2025",
  "scope": "state:ks",
  "title": "HB 2437 (2025-2026 biennium (2026 Regular Session)): HB 2437 Establishing the save Kansas act, authorizing the use of additional resources for verifying voter registration records, imposing restrictions on websites that can accept and transmit voter registration applications, removing individuals disqualified for voting from such records and providing an open records request exemption for certain information related to such records.",
  "urls": [
    "https://www.kslegislature.gov/b2025_26/bills/HB2437/",
    "https://www.kslegislature.gov/b2025_26/bills/download/?apn=b2025_26/year2/ready_for_publication/hb_2437/hb2437_enrolled.pdf",
    "https://www.kslegislature.gov/b2025_26/bills/download/?apn=b2025_26/year2/ready_for_publication/hb_2437/hb2437_00_0000.pdf",
    "https://www.kslegislature.gov/b2025_26/bills/download/?apn=b2025_26/year2/ready_for_publication/hb_2437/hb2437_01_0000.pdf",
    "https://www.kslegislature.gov/b2025_26/bills/download/?apn=b2025_26/year2/ready_for_publication/ccr_2026_hb2437_s_4538.pdf"
  ],
  "version": "enrolled",
  "operative_text": "(a_in_person_id) not stated.\n(b_no_id_remedy) not stated.\n(c_mail_ballot_id) not stated.\n(d_proof_of_citizenship)\n(section) K.S.A. 25-2324(a) as amended (Sec. 10), enrolled\n(quote) The county election officer shall notify any person removed from the voter registration rolls that the person may be reinstated on the voter registration rolls by providing proof of their citizenship.\n(e_other_rule)\n(section) New Sec. 2(a) (SAVE checks), enrolled\n(quote) (a) The secretary of state shall: (1) Conduct two checks each calendar year to compare the statewide voter registration system against SAVE; (2) ensure that one check is completed not later than 180 days before a regularly scheduled federal general election; and (3) transmit any potential noncitizen matches to the appropriate county election official for immediate review.\n(section) New Sec. 2(b), enrolled\n(quote) (b) Upon receipt of such information from the secretary of state, the county election officer shall: (1) Notify the voter pursuant to the national voter registration act requirements before any voter registration cancellation occurs; (2) place the voter in challenged or pending verification status until resolution; (3) require confirmation of the identified voter's citizenship status; and (4) remove from the voter rolls any individual who is confirmed to be ineligible.\n(other) New Sec. 1: names the act the SAVE Kansas act and defines SAVE, statewide voter registration system, election official.\n(other) New Sec. 3-4: annual SAVE report to legislative committees; secure handling of SAVE data.\n(other) Other sections (restrictions on websites that accept voter registration applications, quarterly reports of noncitizen benefit recipients, removal of disqualified individuals, open-records exemption) are not about ID or proof of citizenship and were not quoted. Quotes are copied from the PDF text layer; strike-through and underline marking is not visible in extracted text, so reprinted existing law and new wording cannot be told apart from the quote alone.",
